From: Michael R Sweet <msweet@msweet.org>
Date: Tue, 05 Apr 2026 14:44:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Range check job-password-supported (CVE-2026-39314)

Backport of upstream OpenPrinting/cups commit
3d748da980e995cb51b71e80eeba21b223ebcf7c (2.4.x release line
equivalent 928a86b1 series, first shipped in v2.4.17) -
CVE-2026-39314 / GHSA-pp8w-2g52-7vj7:
_ppdCreateFromIPP() read the attacker-controlled
job-password-supported integer with an upper clamp only.  A negative
value, converted to size_t for memset() of the stack-local
pattern[33] buffer, smashed the root cupsd stack (remote DoS / memory
corruption) whenever a PPD was generated from a malicious IPP
printer's Get-Printer-Attributes response (everywhere queue creation).

Fix: enter the password/pattern block only when the value is > 0 -
verbatim one-line condition from upstream (the upstream
copyright-year hunk is cosmetic and omitted).

Adaptation: this port names the function _ppdCreateFromIPP2 and
earlier chain patches shift the block to line 3531; context lines are
otherwise byte-identical.  Generated and verified against the full
install.py chain (git apply in post-chain build state).

Upstream-commit: 3d748da980e995cb51b71e80eeba21b223ebcf7c
CVE: CVE-2026-39314
GHSA: GHSA-pp8w-2g52-7vj7

diff --git a/cups/ppd-cache.c b/cups/ppd-cache.c
index 88c1e250..32ec7786 100644
--- a/cups/ppd-cache.c
+++ b/cups/ppd-cache.c
@@ -3531,7 +3531,7 @@ _ppdCreateFromIPP2(
   * Password/PIN printing...
   */
 
-  if ((attr = ippFindAttribute(supported, "job-password-supported", IPP_TAG_INTEGER)) != NULL)
+  if ((attr = ippFindAttribute(supported, "job-password-supported", IPP_TAG_INTEGER)) != NULL && ippGetInteger(attr, 0) > 0)
   {
     char	pattern[33];		/* Password pattern */
     int		maxlen = ippGetInteger(attr, 0);
